 a fixed amplitude, frequency and height over an electrochemically active sample in solution measuring and mapping the electric field generated by the sample. This technique is used to probe the nature of corrosion processes.","Class Name":"scanning vibrating electrode technique","Detailed Ontology":"chmo","Is Defining Ontology":true,"Mapped Term IRI":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHMO_0002712","Mapped Term Label":"scanning vibrating electrode technique","Mapped Term Ontology":"chmo","Match Type":"SEARCH_RESULT","Score":0.75,"Short Form":"CHMO_0002712","Source":"Zooma","Zooma Confidence":"GOOD"},{"Class Definition":"The time that an analyzer started a scan, relative to the start of the MS run.","Class Name":"scan start time","Detailed Ontology":"ms","Is Defining Ontology":true,"Mapped Term IRI":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MS_1000016","Mapped Term Label":"scan start time","Mapped Term Ontology":"ms","Match Type":"SEARCH_RESULT","Score":0.75,"Short Form":"MS_1000016","Source":"Zooma","Zooma Confidence":"GOOD"},{"Class Definition":"Microscopy where a laser is scanned over the surface of the specimen and the photocurrent is recorded as a function of position.","Class Name":"scanning photocurrent microscopy","Detailed Ontology":"chmo","Is Defining Ontology":true,"Mapped Term IRI":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHMO_0002553","Mapped Term Label":"scanning photocurrent microscopy","Mapped Term Ontology":"chmo","Match Type":"SEARCH_RESULT","Score":0.75,"Short Form":"CHMO_0002553","Source":"Zooma","Zooma Confidence":"GOOD"},{"Class Definition":"An image obtained by scanning a gas (Ar or Kr) laser spot of specific wavelength over the specimen and collecting the light emitted by chromophores in the specimen (fluorescence) using a system of magnifying lenses. The fluorescence passes through a pinhole before it reaches the lenses, allowing only light from the focal point to pass to the detector, reducing background interference.","Class Name":"confocal laser scanning micrograph","Detailed Ontology":"chmo","Is Defining Ontology":true,"Mapped Term IRI":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHMO_0002601","Mapped Term Label":"confocal laser scanning micrograph","Mapped Term Ontology":"chmo","Match Type":"SEARCH_RESULT","Score":0.75,"Short Form":"CHMO_0002601","Source":"Zooma","Zooma Confidence":"GOOD"},{"Class Definition":"A technique of diagnostic imaging of RETINA or CORNEA of the human eye involving the measurement and interpretation of polarizing ELECTROMAGNETIC WAVES such as radio or light waves. It is helpful in the diagnosis of GLAUCOMA; MACULAR DEGENERATION; and other retinal disorders.","Class Name":"Scanning Laser Polarimetry","Detailed Ontology":"mesh","Is Defining Ontology":true,"Mapped Term IRI":"http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D057109","Mapped Term Label":"Scanning Laser Polarimetry","Mapped Term Ontology":"mesh","Match Type":"SEARCH_RESULT","Score":0.75,"Short Form":"mesh_D057109","Source":"Zooma","Zooma Confidence":"GOOD"},{"Class Definition":"","Class Name":"Scanning Laser Polarimetry","Detailed Ontology":"omit","Is Defining Ontology":true,"Mapped Term IRI":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMIT_0026859","Mapped Term Label":"Scanning Laser Polarimetry","Mapped Term Ontology":"omit","Match Type":"SEARCH_RESULT","Score":0.75,"Short Form":"OMIT_0026859","Source":"Zooma","Zooma Confidence":"GOOD"},{"Class Definition":"A type of confocal microscopy evidence that results in an image that is built up pixel-by-pixel by collecting the emitted photons from the fluorophores in the sample by passing a laser beam through a light source aperture which is then focused by an objective lens into a small area on the surface of the sample.","Class Name":"confocal laser scanning microscopy evidence","Detailed Ontology":"eco","Is Defining Ontology":true,"Mapped Term IRI":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECO_0007059","Mapped Term Label":"confocal laser scanning microscopy evidence","Mapped Term Ontology":"eco","Match Type":"SEARCH_RESULT","Score":0.75,"Sho